{
  "_comment": "PAPER-CLAIMS LEDGER. One entry per quantitative claim that a research note proposed importing into this stack. claims.py turns each entry into either (a) a check against an artifact on disk, or (b) a REFUSAL naming what is missing. There is deliberately no third option: a claim with neither a check nor a reason code is a hard error, so the ledger cannot quietly shrink. Coverage is reported as counts by outcome, never as a percentage.",

  "_provenance_warning": "THE SOURCE NOTES ARE NOT IN THIS REPO. The six notes (blackwell-fp4, moe-serving, longctx, decode-systems, specdec, our-models) were supplied to a survey agent in-context on 2026-08-10 and were never written to disk; `grep -rl 'SwiftSpec|AcceptMoE|RocketKV|BitsMoE|SageAttention3' <repo>` returns nothing. Every `claim_text` below is therefore RELAYED, not quoted from an artifact, and `note_artifact` is null for all 30 entries. claims.py prints this as a standing refusal (NOTE-CORPUS-ABSENT) on every run. What the ledger can still check with teeth is the subset of claims that are assertions ABOUT OUR OWN pinned artifacts -- those are decidable from disk no matter who said them, and they are where four of the five contradictions live.",

  "_outcomes": {
    "CONTRADICTED": "the claim, evaluated at our operating point against an artifact on disk, is false",
    "BOUNDED_BELOW_CLAIM": "the claim's mechanism is capped by an artifact-derived bound that is strictly below the claimed factor",
    "CONSISTENT": "the claim survives every bound the artifacts support; NOT an endorsement",
    "NOT_COMPARABLE": "different hardware / model / batch regime / unformalized phase -- no comparison is manufactured",
    "REFUSED": "the ledger cannot decide because a named artifact is missing; exit non-zero"
  },

  "_reason_codes": {
    "NO_CHECKPOINT": "the checkpoint the claim is anchored to is not pinned on this box",
    "NO_EVAL_ARTIFACT": "a quality/accuracy claim with no committed eval output to compare against",
    "DIFFERENT_HARDWARE": "measured on a part we do not have; no transfer argument exists",
    "PHASE_NOT_FORMALIZED": "the phase has no traffic manifest or measured wall in this repo",
    "TRAINING_GATED": "requires retraining; not evaluable from an inference artifact",
    "NEEDS_MEASURED_ARTIFACT": "bound exists but its measured constant's artifact is deleted",
    "NEEDS_MACHINE_CONSTANT": "bound needs a datasheet constant absent from machine.json",
    "NEEDS_MOE_PHASE_MANIFEST": "bound needs expert-aware phases in kernels.json; gen.py die()s on MoE today"
  },

